 =====================================================================
 Power BI Data Modeling
 All measures live in the "total" table.
 =====================================================================


 =====================================================================
 1. SALES METRICS
 Source: fact_sales (grain = one row per order line)
 =====================================================================

 Total revenue from all order lines
 total_sales = SUM(fact_sales[line_total])

 Number of unique orders (distinct count, because the table is line-grain)
 total_orders = DISTINCTCOUNT(fact_sales[order_id])


 =====================================================================
 2. CUSTOMER METRICS
 Sources: dim_customer, fact_sales
 =====================================================================

 All customers in the customer dimension
 base_total_customers = COUNT(dim_customer[Customer_Id])

 Customers who have placed orders (counted by bill-to city key)
 totalactive_costomers = DISTINCTCOUNT(fact_sales[billtothecity_key])


 =====================================================================
 3. FULFILLMENT METRICS
 Source: fact_order_fullfillment (accumulating snapshot, one row per order)
 =====================================================================

 Average days from order date to payment date
 avg_order_to_pay_days = AVERAGE(fact_order_fullfillment[order_to_pay])
